{"name":"Cocoon","hex":"#dedbcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cocoon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The silky case spun by the larvae of some insects in which they metamorphose, protecting the pupa within.","Any similar protective case."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To envelop in a protective case.","To withdraw into such a case."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cocoon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cocoon Recordings","blocks":[{"text":"Cocoon Recordings is a record label founded in 2000 and operated by DJ and electronic music producer Sven Väth. Based in Frankfurt, Germany, Cocoon is a division of the Cocoon Music Event GmbH."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/Cocoon_Rec_Logo.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoon_Recordings","wikidata":"Q322738"},{"title":"Cocoon (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Cocoon is a French pop-folk band from Clermont-Ferrand (France) that sings in English. It was created in 2006 by Mark Daumail, alongside Morgane Imbeaud. They released the albums My Friends all Died in a Plane Crash in 2007 and Where the Oceans End in 2010, which were defined by dual lead vocals from both, and by its coupling of mostly upbeat-sounding music and very dark lyrics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Cocoon_%28groupe%29.jpg/330px-Cocoon_%28groupe%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoon_(band)","wikidata":"Q2746889"},{"title":"Cocoon (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cocoon is a 1985 American science fiction comedy drama film directed by Ron Howard and written by Tom Benedek from a story by David Saperstein. The film stars Don Ameche, Wilford Brimley, Hume Cronyn, Brian Dennehy, Jack Gilford, Steve Guttenberg, Maureen Stapleton, Jessica Tandy, Gwen Verdon, Herta Ware, Tahnee Welch, and Linda Harrison, and follows a group of elderly people rejuvenated by aliens."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ef/Cocoonposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoon_(film)","wikidata":"Q1105463"},{"title":"Cocoon (manga)","blocks":[{"text":"Cocoon  is a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by Machiko Kyō. It was serialized in Akita Shoten's josei manga magazine Elegance Eve from March 2009 to May 2010. An anime television film adaptation produced by Sasayuri premiered in March 2025."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Cocoon_manga_volume_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocoon_(manga)","wikidata":"Q119985670"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"cocoon":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/En-us-cocoon.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/fd/En-us-cocoon.ogg/En-us-cocoon.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.456875},{"title":"Cocoon-Shaped Jar Han dynasty","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Cocoon-Shaped_Jar_Han_dynasty.jpg/500px-Cocoon-Shaped_Jar_Han_dynasty.jpg","ratio":1.2578616352201257,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocoon-Shaped_Jar_Han_dynasty.jpg","share":0.25375},{"title":"Mode Gakuen Cocoon Tower, Tokyo, West view 20190419 1","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Mode_Gakuen_Cocoon_Tower%2C_Tokyo%2C_West_view_20190419_1.jpg/500px-Mode_Gak